Revision history for browser

0.155 2026-09-22
 - refactored lib/Browser/Runner/NodeRuntime.pm's 12 near-identical
   required-argument guards (my $x = $args{x} || die "x is
   required";, repeated across 3 distinct argument names -
   home_root x7, package_json x4, module x1) to share one new
   _required_arg helper, centralizing the message format in one
   place. Pure refactor, no behavior change: verified by the full
   existing NodeRuntime test suite (17 files, 272 assertions) passing
   unchanged before and after. CORRECTION during drafting: the
   initial grep for this ticket's own scope found only 11 occurrences
   (missing the distinct 'module is required' guard); a broader
   re-grep before writing any code caught the true count of 12 and
   the refactor covers all of them. Found during a scheduled
   improvement hunt (JOB-004), the second pure maintainability-
   refactor ticket this session after D2B-178 (D2B-179)

0.154 2026-09-22
 - refactored lib/Browser/Search.pm's 3 engine parsers (_parse_bing,
   _parse_google, _parse_duckduckgo), which were each structurally
   identical except for their own regex, to share one new
   _parse_with_regex helper - reducing 3 copies of the same
   loop/build/rank logic to 1. Pure refactor, no behavior change:
   verified by the full existing search test suite (17 files, 126
   assertions covering all 3 parsers, entity-decode, dedup-pinning,
   fallback logic) passing unchanged before and after. Self-caught
   and fixed a real regression mid-implementation: the first version
   dropped the /s regex modifier when moving each pattern from an
   inline eval to a qr{} interpolated into the shared helper - a
   qr{} does not inherit an outer match's /s flag, so multi-line
   HTML briefly stopped matching, caught by re-running the full
   suite (not just a subset) before considering the work done. Found
   during a scheduled improvement hunt (JOB-004), the first pure
   maintainability-refactor ticket this session, distinct from its
   many bug/coverage/doc-gap tickets (D2B-178)

0.153 2026-09-22
 - added lib/Browser/Runner/VersionCompare.pm to docs/overview.md's
   Delivery section, which had drifted since D2B-155 (this session)
   extracted it from NodeRuntime.pm - SKILLS.md and README.md were
   both updated at the time, but docs/overview.md's separate,
   differently-worded Delivery bullet was missed. Added a new
   regression test that globs lib/Browser/Runner/*.pm and asserts
   every file is named somewhere in docs/overview.md, guarding
   against this class of drift recurring for any current or future
   module. No behavioral change. Found by direct doc-file
   investigation after 2 consecutive fork-hunts (search _rank edge
   cases, BrowserPath.pm Windows env-var handling) returned genuinely
   clean results (D2B-177)

0.152 2026-09-22
 - extended lib/Browser/Search.pm's %NAMED_ENTITIES with 11 common
   typographic entities realistically found in real search-engine
   snippet/title text: nbsp, mdash, ndash, lsquo, rsquo, ldquo, rdquo,
   hellip, copy, trade, reg. Previously only amp/lt/gt/quot/apos
   (D2B-050) plus numeric/hex references and surrogate pairs (D2B-054)
   were decoded - every other named entity, including these common
   ones, leaked through as literal entity text into browser.search's
   JSON output. Verified directly in Docker before the fix that all
   9 tested entities were unchanged; genuine red-green TDD (9 of 12
   new assertions failed pre-fix). Updated README.md/docs/usage.md's
   entity lists to match. Found by a fork-hunt during D2B-175's
   pipeline-continuity gate, investigating entity-decoding gaps and
   _strip_tags's nested/malformed-markup handling (the latter checked
   and found clean) (D2B-176)

0.151 2026-09-22
 - documented and pinned browser.search's existing behavior of not
   deduplicating result entries that share an identical URL (a
   realistic collision on a real search page, e.g. an ad slot
   alongside its matching organic result). No test anywhere exercised
   this before now; verified directly in Docker that a 3-block bing-
   style body with entries 1 and 3 sharing a URL returns all 3
   entries via _parse_bing, un-deduplicated - each still consumes its
   own --max slot. This is deliberately left as a documented
   limitation rather than a code change - whether to actually
   deduplicate is a product decision for the owner, not decided here.
   Added t/175-d2b-175-search-duplicate-url-no-dedup.t; updated
   README.md and docs/usage.md's Search Mode sections. No behavioral
   change. Found by a fork-hunt during D2B-174's pipeline-continuity
   gate, investigating search result-count/pagination edge cases; a
   parallel angle (engine_used/engines_tried consistency) was checked
   and ruled out by construction (D2B-175)

0.150 2026-09-22
 - corrected an overstated comment in
   t/29-d2b-032-tag-name-must-match.t claiming a body with no
   explicit text/html content-type is now always escaped/wrapped -
   true only for fragment-shaped bodies. lib/Browser/Runner.pm's
   _response_document also has 2 unconditional body-prefix bypass
   checks (a body starting with a boundary-checked <!doctype html> or
   <html> tag) that trust the body raw regardless of the declared
   content-type - already documented in README.md edge case 6, but
   untested and easily missed by the fragment-focused comment. Added
   t/174-d2b-174-html-tag-prefix-bypass.t pinning both the bypass and
   the contrasting non-bypass case (a non-html-tag-shaped body is
   still wrapped). No behavioral change. Found by a fork-hunt during
   D2B-173's pipeline-continuity gate; the fork's own initial framing
   (an application/xml example) did not actually hold up under
   independent re-verification, but led to this narrower, verified
   gap (D2B-174)

0.149 2026-09-22
 - taught _is_captcha_page (lib/Browser/Runner.pm) to recognize
   Cloudflare's own interstitial/block pages: "Just a moment..." (its
   JS-challenge page) and "Attention Required! | Cloudflare" (its
   block page for flagged traffic). Neither used the word "captcha"
   nor any recognized reCAPTCHA/hCaptcha widget markup, so they were
   previously invisible to this skill's anti-bot-wall detection - a
   real behavior change, unlike this session's recent coverage-only
   tickets. Added t/173-d2b-173-cloudflare-challenge-detection.t
   (genuine red-green TDD: 2 of 3 assertions failed before the fix).
   Updated README.md and docs/usage.md's captcha-detection phrase
   lists to match; SKILLS.md has no phrase-enumerating section to
   extend. All existing captcha-detection tests (including the D2B-083
   false-positive regression) continue to pass unchanged. Found by a
   fork-hunt during D2B-172's pipeline-continuity gate, investigating
   captcha-detection edge cases (D2B-173)

0.148 2026-09-22
 - documented and tested the "0 disables the timeout" caveat for
   browser.get/post/png's --timeout-ms flag: Playwright's goto()
   treats timeout: 0 as disabling the navigation timeout entirely,
   not "instant" - a literal reading of --timeout-ms 0 can genuinely
   hang. This was already documented for browser.search in SKILLS.md
   but absent for get/post/png, and nowhere in README.md/docs/usage.md
   for either command. Added matching notes to all 3 doc files and a
   new regression test asserting _goto_options(timeout_ms => 0)
   produces timeout => 0, distinct from the existing test covering a
   positive override value. No behavioral change. Found by a fork-hunt
   during D2B-171's pipeline-continuity gate, investigating
   timeout/retry semantics (D2B-172)

0.147 2026-09-22
 - closed the untested missing-HOME guard in
   lib/Browser/Runner/NodeRuntime.pm's _ensure_node_runtime - the
   exact sibling of D2B-170's Runner.pm::_jquery_path finding in the
   sister module. No behavioral change - the guard already does the
   right thing. Added t/171-d2b-171-noderuntime-missing-home.t. Found
   by directly grepping every "|| die"/"or die" guard across
   lib/Browser/*.pm and lib/Browser/Runner/*.pm and cross-checking
   each against t/*.t for coverage, immediately after D2B-170 shipped
   (D2B-171)

0.146 2026-09-22
 - closed the untested missing-HOME guard in
   lib/Browser/Runner.pm's _jquery_path: it reads $ENV{HOME} and dies
   with "HOME is required for browser skill jQuery injection" before
   ever checking whether jquery.min.js exists there. Both existing
   tests for this sub always set $ENV{HOME} to a temp directory first,
   so this die branch had zero coverage. No behavioral change - the
   branch already does the right thing. Added a new assertion in
   t/04-runner-unit.t beside the 2 existing _jquery_path tests. Found
   by following up a lead from a fork-hunt during D2B-169's
   pipeline-continuity gate (--data JSON parsing and browser-cleanup
   angles, both clean) that suggested checking _run_get/_run_png's
   surrounding code more closely (D2B-170)

0.145 2026-09-22
 - closed the untested Getopt::Long ambiguous-abbreviation error path
   in lib/Browser/CLI.pm's execute_search: --engine and --engines both
   start with "engine", so an abbreviation matching both (e.g. --e)
   triggers Getopt::Long's own ambiguity detection. execute_search
   already surfaced this correctly via its existing "Invalid options:
   ..." die, giving exit code 2 - the shared exit-2 convention this
   session already documented (D2B-139/145/147/148/149/150) - but the
   path had zero test coverage. No behavioral change. Added
   t/169-d2b-169-search-ambiguous-engine-abbreviation.t. Found by a
   5th fork-hunt during D2B-167's pipeline-continuity gate,
   investigating Getopt::Long CLI argument-parsing edge cases; a
   parallel dead-code/unused-subroutine sweep found nothing (D2B-169)

0.144 2026-09-22
 - closed the one remaining untested branch in
   lib/Browser/Runner.pm's _run_controller_script: the compile-time
   eval that builds a controller-mode --script (--playwright/--agent
   /--flow) into a closure (line ~297-306). Only its sibling
   runtime-die branch (script compiles, then dies when called) had a
   regression test; a syntactically-invalid --script had none.
   Verified in Docker that the branch already behaves correctly -
   reporting "Controller script failed: syntax error..." distinctly
   from the runtime-die case. Branch coverage on Runner.pm rose from
   97.8% to 98.9%. No behavioral change. Added
   t/167-d2b-167-controller-script-syntax-error.t. Found by a 4th
   fork-hunt during D2B-166's pipeline-continuity gate, after 3 prior
   fork-hunts (14 angles, including a full perlsec audit) came up
   empty (D2B-167)

0.143 2026-09-22
 - fixed a documentation gap: D2B-158's --script must-not-be-empty
   refusal (shipped this session) had zero mentions in SKILLS.md,
   README.md, or docs/usage.md, unlike D2B-156 (documented) and
   D2B-157 (covered generically by existing wording). Added matching
   notes to all 3 doc files stating an explicit empty --script is
   refused with "--script must not be empty" in both plain and
   controller mode, while omitting --script entirely remains an
   unaffected silent no-op. No code touched. New regression test at
   t/166-d2b-166-script-empty-doc-accuracy.t. Found by a fork-hunt
   doing a fresh SKILLS.md-accuracy sweep after the branch-coverage
   vein (D2B-160-165) was confirmed exhausted (D2B-166)

0.142 2026-09-22
 - closed 2 reachable branches in
   lib/Browser/Runner/VersionCompare.pm found by a branch-coverage
   sweep extending the D2B-160/161/162/163/164 pattern:
   version_satisfies_spec's top-of-function undef/empty-string guard
   for its 2 arguments (never triggered by any of the 11 existing call
   sites), and its !@installed-or-!@minimum guard, reachable under a
   caret-range spec when the installed version string does not start
   with digits (e.g. version_satisfies_spec('abc', '^1.2.3')). Branch
   coverage was 93.3% before this ticket. Added direct-call regression
   tests at t/165-d2b-165-versioncompare-remaining-branches.t proving
   both branches already work correctly. No behavioral change. Found
   by a fork-hunt during D2B-164's pipeline-continuity gate, with the
   finding re-verified in Docker after the fork-hunt's own honest
   uncertainty flag about one of the two branches (D2B-165)

0.141 2026-09-22
 - closed 4 reachable branch groups in lib/Browser/Runner.pm found by a
   branch-coverage sweep extending the D2B-160/161/162/163 pattern:
   _run_png's missing-directory creation (make_path), _run_png's
   $response-falsy degradation of headers/status, _is_captcha_page's
   "verify you are human" phrase (the only one of 4 captcha phrases
   never directly tested), and _response_document's undef-body
   default. Branch coverage was 92.3% before this ticket. Added
   direct-call/mock regression tests at
   t/164-d2b-164-runner-remaining-branches.t proving each branch group
   already works correctly. No behavioral change. Two lower-value
   lines (76, 306 - I/O-close-failure and eval-failure branches) were
   deliberately left untouched, matching the same convention already
   established for NodeRuntime.pm. Found by a fork-hunt during
   D2B-163's pipeline-continuity gate (D2B-164)

0.140 2026-09-22
 - closed 3 reachable-but-untested branches in lib/Browser/CLI.pm found
   by a branch-coverage sweep extending the D2B-160/161/162 pattern to
   CLI.pm: execute()'s Unsupported method guard, execute()'s
   Unexpected arguments guard, and execute_search()'s own copy of the
   same Unexpected arguments guard. Branch coverage was 92.8% before
   this ticket. Added 3 direct-call regression tests at
   t/163-d2b-163-cli-remaining-branches.t proving each guard already
   works correctly. No behavioral change - the guards were already
   functionally correct. Runner.pm's own smaller branch-coverage gap
   (92.3%, mixed reachability) was investigated less deeply and left
   for a possible future ticket. Found by a fork-hunt during D2B-162's
   pipeline-continuity gate (D2B-163)

0.139 2026-09-22
 - improved lib/Browser/Runner/BrowserPath.pm's branch coverage from
   85.7% to 94.6%, following the D2B-160/161 pattern: a branch-coverage
   sweep across the remaining lib/ modules (CLI.pm=92.8, Runner.pm=
   92.3, NodeRuntime.pm=76.8, BrowserPath.pm=85.7, VersionCompare.pm=
   93.3) found BrowserPath.pm's gap was reachable via direct calls,
   unlike NodeRuntime.pm's larger gap (mostly low-value filesystem-
   open-failure branches, left untouched, same convention already
   established for that class of path). Added direct-call tests for
   _browser_path_is_usable's and _find_in_path's undef/empty/
   relative-path rejection guards and _command_lookup_names' Windows
   already-has-extension branch (using the existing local $^O =
   'MSWin32' test pattern). The seen-path dedup guard's true branch
   (3 sites) turned out impractical to force without complex
   filesystem mocking - documented instead with a comment explaining
   why, rather than an artificial test. New regression test at
   t/162-d2b-162-browserpath-remaining-branches.t. No behavioral
   change. Found by the main session's own Devel::Cover branch sweep
   after a fork-hunt got stuck in a wait loop (D2B-162)

0.138 2026-09-22
 - closed the 4 remaining untested branches in lib/Browser/Search.pm
   that D2B-160 identified but explicitly left out of scope: the
   empty-error-message fallback ('unknown error') in search()'s
   request-failure path; _parse_results' undef-body default to the
   empty string; _strip_tags' undef-value early return; and
   _decode_entities' unknown-named-entity fallback (leaves it
   unescaped). Verified via Devel::Cover -coverage branch that all 4
   were genuinely uncovered before this ticket (branch coverage
   unchanged at 92.0% since D2B-160). Added 4 direct-call regression
   tests at t/161-d2b-161-search-remaining-branches.t proving each
   branch already does the right thing - no code change, no
   behavioral change. Found by a fork-hunt verifying D2B-160's own
   fold-back-flagged follow-up items (D2B-161)

0.137 2026-09-22
 - fixed an undocumented defensive-duplication gap: 3 validation guards
   in Browser::Search::search() (Missing query, At least one engine is
   required, --max must not be negative) were unreachable through
   Browser::CLI::execute_search() (which has its own earlier copies of
   the same 3 checks) and had neither a comment nor a direct test
   proving they were intentional, unlike this same file's own D2B-130
   precedent for an identical situation. Verified via Devel::Cover
   -coverage branch: lib/Browser/Search.pm sat at branch=86.0 despite
   stmt=100.0/sub=100.0 - this project's coverage gate never measures
   branch coverage, so the gap was invisible all session. Added a
   D2B-130-style comment above each guard and 3 direct-call regression
   tests at t/160-d2b-160-search-guards-direct-call.t proving each
   guard works correctly for any caller bypassing execute_search(). No
   behavior change - the guards were already functionally correct.
   Found by a fork-hunt's deep branch-coverage review, after a first
   fork-hunt attempt found nothing and a second, broader one turned up
   this finding (D2B-160)

0.136 2026-09-22
 - fixed a documentation drift: README.md and docs/usage.md's
   URL-missing-check claim still described the pre-D2B-156 behavior
   ("only refused as missing when it is truly absent or an empty
   string"), never updated when D2B-156 (this session) widened
   lib/Browser/CLI.pm:214's check to also refuse a whitespace-only URL.
   Updated both lines to state the current, complete rule (undefined,
   empty-string, or whitespace-only are all refused), keeping the
   existing "0 is accepted" clarification unchanged. No code touched.
   New regression test at
   t/159-d2b-159-url-missing-doc-accuracy.t. Found by a fork-hunt
   doing a documentation-accuracy check after the validation-asymmetry
   pattern was confirmed exhausted this cycle (D2B-159)

0.135 2026-09-22
 - fixed an input-validation inconsistency: Browser::Runner::_run_script
   (lib/Browser/Runner.pm) only checked !defined $args{script} before
   falling through to $page->evaluate('') in plain (non-controller)
   mode, so an explicit empty-string --script value silently evaluated
   an empty script instead of being refused - unlike controller mode's
   _run_controller_script, which already refuses the same empty value
   with "Controller mode requires --script". Added a matching die in
   the plain-mode branch. Omitting --script entirely remains an
   unaffected no-op. New regression test at
   t/158-d2b-158-script-empty-string-refused.t. Found by a fork-hunt
   during D2B-157's pipeline-continuity gate, after --engine/--engines/
   --file/--data/--timeout-ms were all checked for the same asymmetry
   and found already correct (D2B-158)

0.134 2026-09-22
 - fixed an input-validation inconsistency: --browser's default
   handling (lib/Browser/Runner/BrowserPath.pm) used
   $args{browser} || 'chrome', which silently coerced an explicit
   empty-string --browser value to the default instead of refusing it
   - unlike --wait-until's already-established precedent
   (lib/Browser/Runner.pm), which distinguishes "not given" from
   "given but empty" and dies on the latter. Changed to
   defined($args{browser}) ? $args{browser} : 'chrome', letting the
   existing Unsupported-browser-type check naturally reject an empty
   string. Omitting --browser entirely still defaults to chrome
   unchanged. New regression test at
   t/157-d2b-157-browser-empty-string-refused.t. Found by a fork-hunt
   during D2B-156's pipeline-continuity gate, after the private-sub,
   file-size-decomposition, and URL-validation-asymmetry patterns were
   all independently exhausted (D2B-157)

0.133 2026-09-22
 - fixed an input-validation inconsistency: browser.get/post/png's
   "Missing URL" check (lib/Browser/CLI.pm:214) only rejected an
   undefined or exactly-empty-string URL, unlike browser.search's
   "Missing query" check 3 lines away (line 288), which already used a
   whitespace-only regex. A whitespace-only URL passed through
   untouched and reached Playwright as a literal URL instead of being
   refused cleanly. Changed line 214 to the same /\A\s*\z/ pattern
   browser.search already uses. The literal URL "0" (D2B-025) remains
   correctly accepted. New regression test at
   t/156-d2b-156-whitespace-url-missing.t. Found by a fork-hunt during
   D2B-155's pipeline-continuity gate, after the private-sub and
   file-size decomposition patterns were both independently verified
   exhausted (D2B-156)

0.132 2026-09-22
 - decomposed lib/Browser/Runner/NodeRuntime.pm: it had grown to 499
