0.120 2026-09-21
 - broadened a doc scope gap left by D2B-138: that ticket documented the
   --help/--version argv pre-parse collision only for browser.post --data,
   but Browser::CLI's _argv_requests_help/_argv_requests_version scan the
   entire raw argv for a standalone --help/--version element before any
   flag's value is assigned by Getopt::Long, so the exact same collision
   applies to every string-valued flag on all four commands - --script,
   --browser, --wait-until, --file (get/post/png), --engine, --engines
   (search), and --data itself. Live-verified via Docker:
   Browser::CLI::execute(method=>'GET', argv=>['URL','--script','--help'])
   returns help text instead of running --script. Broadened the existing
   note in README.md, docs/usage.md, and SKILLS.md to name the general
   rule, with the equals-form (--flag=--help) explicitly called out as
   unaffected. Added a new t/ test asserting the broadened doc wording
   plus a direct behavioral check on _argv_requests_help/_argv_requests_version
   using --script/--browser (not --data), mirroring D2B-138's own test
   pattern. No code change - the pre-parse scan itself remains a separate,
