0.115 2026-09-21
 - fixed a real bug introduced by D2B-134's own security hardening: since that fix started atomically reserving browser.png's default screenshot placeholder via File::Temp with UNLINK => 0, a failure anywhere after that reservation (script/jquery execution, or Playwright's own screenshot() call) left the empty placeholder file orphaned under the system tmpdir forever - UNLINK => 0 deliberately disables File::Temp's own automatic exit-time cleanup. _run_png now wraps every step after reservation - the --file-directory validation, make_path, script/jquery execution, and the screenshot() call itself - in one eval, and, only when it was the one that reserved the default path (never for an explicit --file, which this skill never deletes), unlinks it before re-dying. Full TDD cycle (red/green - a forced script failure confirms no orphaned browser-*.png file remains under tmpdir, and a parallel test confirms a pre-existing user-supplied --file survives a failure with its content untouched). 100% coverage on lib/Browser/Runner.pm. Found by a Codex code-review round deferred from D2B-134 (D2B-135)

0.114 2026-09-21
 - security hardening: browser.png's default screenshot path (no --file given) was previously only ever computed as a hash-derived string under the system tmpdir - it was never actually created by this process before Playwright's screenshot() call opened and wrote to it, leaving a window where another process (or an attacker able to predict the non-cryptographic time()/pid/rand() inputs) could pre-create a symlink or file at that exact path first. _screenshot_path's default branch now reserves the path atomically and exclusively via File::Temp::tempfile (O_CREAT|O_EXCL under the hood) before returning it, closing the initial name-prediction/pre-creation window - Playwright's screenshot() call still overwrites the reserved placeholder file exactly as before. This does not eliminate every theoretical race (a same-UID actor could still unlink-and-replace the reserved file between this process's close() and Playwright's later open()), but it does close the specific gap this ticket targeted: a bare computed pathname that was never actually created by this process at all. The random component's own character set changed from strictly hex (from the old SHA-256-derived name) to File::Temp's own alphanumeric set; the existing filename-shape test was updated to match. Full TDD cycle (red/green). 100% coverage on lib/Browser/Runner.pm. Found by a Codex code-review round during D2B-133 (D2B-134)

0.113 2026-09-21
 - cleanup: _screenshot_path's default-filename entropy join included a stray anonymous empty hashref literal ({}) alongside time(), $$, and rand() - it stringified to a raw memory address with no comment or test explaining why it was there, reading like an accidental leftover rather than a deliberate entropy choice. Removed it and added a comment naming the three genuine entropy sources that remain. No intended API or filename-format behavior change - the generated filename's own value will differ from before (its SHA-256 input changed), but its shape (browser-[A-Fa-f0-9]{16}.png) and everything downstream that depends on it are unaffected, and the existing filename-shape test still passes unchanged. Found by a scheduled hunt (D2B-133)

