0.111 2026-09-21
 - fixed a real bug: browser.png silently accepted --script and --jquery but never ran them - _run_png never called _interact_and_run_script the way _run_get and _run_post both do, so a script (e.g. to dismiss a cookie banner or scroll to an element before capturing) or jQuery injection had no effect at all, with no error or warning. _run_png now calls _interact_and_run_script before taking the screenshot, mirroring browser.get/browser.post exactly, and includes script_result in the PNG result when --script is given - a --script/--jquery failure (a JS error, or a missing jQuery runtime) now causes browser.png to fail with that error too, exactly as browser.get/browser.post already do, whereas before it could never fail this way since the options were never actually run. Following a code-review round, --file's own existing-directory validation was kept ahead of the script/jquery step, so a bad --file still fails fast without ever running a script's real side effects against the page. Full TDD cycle (red/green - new tests confirm the script actually runs against the page and jQuery is actually injected before the screenshot, using the same fake-page evaluation/script-tag tracking the GET/POST tests already use). 100% coverage on lib/Browser/Runner.pm. Found by a scheduled hunt, independently live-verified before ticketing, including confirming no existing test or doc explained the silent no-op as intentional (D2B-131)

0.110 2026-09-21
