0.109 2026-09-21
 - fixed a real bug: _run_quiet_command (used to stage/install Node dependencies via npx/npm) could permanently leave the real STDOUT handle discarded if the STDOUT redirect succeeded but the subsequent STDERR redirect then failed and died - every later `print` to STDOUT in that process would silently write into a tempfile that File::Temp's UNLINK => 1 goes on to delete, instead of reaching the user's terminal, until the process exits (STDERR itself was unaffected in this specific failure path, since it was never actually redirected). The redirect-and-run sequence now runs inside its own eval, and on that failure path the real STDOUT/STDERR are restored before the original error is re-died, mirroring the existing eval/capture/restore-then-rethrow pattern already used in this file (_with_node_runtime_lock's flock-release, _install_node_runtime's chdir-restore). Following a code-review round, the two restores were also made independent of each other via a new _restore_std_handle helper: a STDOUT restore failure no longer skips the STDERR restore attempt, and either restore failing now surfaces its own error to the caller instead of being silently lost. Full TDD cycle (red/green - the red test forces the STDERR redirect to fail via a child-process test that overrides the internal tempfile() call, since reproducing this safely means deliberately breaking a real process's STDOUT/STDERR, which cannot be done in the main test process without corrupting its own TAP output). 100% coverage on lib/Browser/Runner/NodeRuntime.pm. Found by a scheduled hunt, independently live-verified before ticketing (D2B-129)

0.108 2026-09-21
 - investigated a real disk-hygiene gap: _clear_installed_node_modules never clears a module directory left over from a dependency later removed from package.json, so it would accumulate indefinitely under $HOME/node_modules (currently latent, since this skill's own dependency set has never shrunk). A first fix (clearing every entry actually present, not just current-spec ones) was caught by Codex review as unsafe: $HOME/node_modules is the user's real home directory, not one this skill exclusively owns, so that approach could destroy an unrelated node_modules tree a user keeps there for something else entirely. Reverted to the original, safe, current-spec-only clearing and documented this as a known, accepted limitation rather than a bug being fixed - a genuinely safe fix would need a persisted install-history manifest, which is a larger change out of scope here. No behavior change shipped; only documentation/comments added explaining the trade-off. Found by a scheduled hunt (D2B-128)

